<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-NZ 125-4 AFTER 4TH DAY VS ENGLAND.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NZ 125-4 AFTER 4TH DAY VS ENGLAND.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ended a rain shortened fourth day of the second cricket test on Sunday at 125 for four wickets, still needing 134 to make England bat again.</p>
<p>Scores: New Zealand 124 (D. Patel 45, D. Gough 5-40, A. Caddick 4-45) and 125 for four wickets (B.Young 56, B.Pocock 45 not out. R.Croft 3-12).</p>
<p>England 383 (N.Hussain 64, G.Thorpe 108, J.Crawley 56, A.Stewart 52, S.Doull 5-75).</p>
